  "summary": "The code currently uses the insecure MD5 algorithm for password hashing, which is highly vulnerable to modern attacks. I have replaced the hashing logic with bcrypt to ensure proper salting and work factors, added input length validation to prevent DoS, and included docstrings for better maintainability.",
  "fixed_code": "import bcrypt\n\ndef hash_password(password: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Hashes a password using bcrypt with automatic salting.\"\"\"\n    if len(password) > 128:\n        raise ValueError(\"Password too long\")\n    return bcrypt.hashpw(password.encode(\"utf-8\"), bcrypt.gensalt()).decode(\"utf-8\")\n\ndef verify_password(password: str, stored_hash: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Verifies a password against a stored bcrypt hash.\"\"\"\n    return bcrypt.checkpw(password.encode(\"utf-8\"), stored_hash.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n\ndef register(users: dict, name: str, password: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Registers a new user with a hashed password.\"\"\"\n    if name in users:\n        raise ValueError(\"user exists\")\n    users[name] = hash_password(password)"
